===Noun===
{{en-noun|-|s}}

# {{lb|en|uncountable}} The act of storing [[goods]]; the state of being [[store]]d.
#: {{ux|en|There's a lot of '''storage''' in the loft.}}
# {{lb|en|usually|countable}} An object or [[place]] in which something is stored.
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=February 1, 2009|author=Staff writers|title=Fires rage as business counts cost|work=w:Herald Sun|url=http://www.news.com.au/heraldsun/story/0,21985,24990626-661,00.html|passage=Melbourne's water '''storages''' plunged by 0.7 per cent in a week, down to 33.1 per cent capacity, as Victoria recorded its second-driest January on record.|accessdate=9 February 2009|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20090203205954/http://www.news.com.au/heraldsun/story/0,21985,24990626-661,00.html|archivedate=3 February 2009}}
#* '''2011''' (2008), Wan Renpu, Petroleum Industry Press (translator), ''Advanced Well Completion Engineering'', [http://books.google.com.au/books?id=GH6JoDxT_9sC&pg=PA115&lpg=PA115&dq=%22storages%22+-intitle:%22%22+-inauthor:%22%22&source=bl&ots=s99om2xr2P&sig=CBT3Z6sdmxEoEeGQOBFgqUuvWqA&hl=en&sa=X&ei=3u1mUN75A-fqiAf7iIHYDw&redir_esc=y#v=onepage&q=%22storages%22%20-intitle%3A%22%22%20-inauthor%3A%22%22&f=false page 115],
#*: Underground natural gas '''storages''' are underground facilities for storing natural gas. At present, there are three types of underground natural gas '''storages''' worldwide, which include depleted oil and gas reservoir gas '''storages''', salt-cave gas '''storages''' and aquifer '''storages'''.
#* '''2012''', A. Grinham, B. Gibbes, D. Gale, M. Watkinson, M. Bartow (University of Queensland), ''Extreme rainfall and drinking water quality: a regional perspective'', C. A. Brebbia, ''Water Pollution XI'', [http://books.google.com.au/books?id=lWt8TKCgMmAC&pg=PA187&lpg=PA187&dq=%22storages%22+-intitle:%22%22+-inauthor:%22%22&source=bl&ots=0Ub0tHGlE3&sig=eh1Ko0rFapy2oN7zkKNXqg2BtWw&hl=en&sa=X&ei=3u1mUN75A-fqiAf7iIHYDw&redir_esc=y#v=onepage&q=%22storages%22%20-intitle%3A%22%22%20-inauthor%3A%22%22&f=false page 187],
#*: Low impact '''storages''' included the northern and southern region′s Cooloolabin Dam, Baroon Pocket Dam, Leslie Harrison Dam, Hinze Dam and Little Nerang Dam. Highly impacted '''storages''' included central region′s Wivenhoe Dam, Somerset Dam and North Pine Dam (Fig. 2), where TSS concentrations in these central '''storages''' where{{sic}} more than double compared to northern and southern '''storages''' (Fig. 2A).
# {{lb|en|usually|uncountable|computer hardware}} Any [[computer]] [[device]], including such as a [[disk]], on which [[data]] is stored for a longer term than [[main memory]].
#: {{ux|en|I′d recommend backing up these files to '''storage''' before reinstalling the operating system.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2007|author=Ramesh Bangia|title=Computer Fundamentals and Information Technology|publisher=Firewall Media|location=India|pageurl=http://books.google.com.au/books?id=mt5lkIS29fQC&pg=PA43&lpg=PA43&dq=%22storages%22+-intitle:%22%22+-inauthor:%22%22&source=bl&ots=re_Gn5b4vU&sig=ZNQ_YHZcDfwTMx-NteD7Jz5_UDw&hl=en&sa=X&ei=3u1mUN75A-fqiAf7iIHYDw&redir_esc=y#v=onepage&q=%22storages%22%20-intitle%3A%22%22%20-inauthor%3A%22%22&f=false|page=43
|passage=Secondary '''storages''' are used to store system programs (viz; operating system, assembler, interpreter, compiler and so on), data files, software packages and so on.}}
# {{lb|en|uncountable}} The [[price]] charged for storing goods.

